THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTIONS
========================

AgileHarness is distributed as SOURCE, and its npm DEPENDENCIES are not
redistributed here — they are fetched from the registry at install time by
whoever builds the project. The attributions for those are informational: they
identify the third-party components whose licenses impose obligations that
survive into a derivative work, so that a fork knows the terms before it bundles
them.

There is one exception, and it is not informational. A few third-party FILES are
checked into this repository, so they travel with every clone, tarball and fork
of it. They are listed under "Redistributed third-party files" below, and the
notices their licenses require live inside the files themselves. That section
carries a legal obligation of its own.

Neither list is decorative — both are measured against the tree on disk, and the
measurement is what keeps this file from drifting into fiction:

  * packages/storymap-ui/src/lib/storymap/oss-license.test.ts walks the real
    dependency closure of `packages/storymap-ui` and fails when a component that
    requires attribution is missing from this file.

  * packages/storymap-ui/src/lib/storymap/vendored-notice.test.ts sweeps the
    files git actually TRACKS, singles out the ones that carry third-party code,
    and fails when one of them is missing from the list below, is listed but no
    longer on disk, or has lost the copyright notice its license requires. It is
    how anyone — a fork, a reviewer, CI — finds out that this section stopped
    being true.


